-- g8-tests-red.l4: THE ASSERTIONS IN THIS FILE ARE MEANT TO FAIL, and there are 16 of them (check.sh lists the count).
--
-- They are the claims of the SimpLEX test table that the Fees Regulations as made and as amended do not meet.  The
-- SimpLEX table was written against the draft, whose numbering of regulation 2 and whose fees differ from both texts
-- that were published (traps T33 and T34).  Each failing claim is a finding:
--   as made (10 claims fail):
--     row 5   a theoretical exam has no fee as made (the amount 273 and the reference 2(a) fail);
--     row 6   the practical-exam fee is regulation 2(a), where the table cites 2(b);
--     row 7   the objection charge is regulation 2(b), where the table cites 2(c); and for an appeal on a THEORETICAL
--             exam there is no charge at all as made (the amount and the reference fail);
--     row 8   for a theoretical exam no fee is fixed, so regulation 4 does not bar it and "suspension of service" is not reached;
--     example the same: "registration rejected, payment must be completed" is not reached for a theoretical exam as made.
--   as amended (6 claims fail):
--     row 5   a theoretical exam costs 158, not 273, and is regulation 2(a1), not 2(a);
--     row 6   the practical-exam fee is regulation 2(a), where the table cites 2(b);
--     row 7   the objection charge is regulation 2(b), where the table cites 2(c); and for an appeal on a PRACTICAL exam
--             there is no charge as amended (the amount and the reference fail).
-- The claims against the draft that hold, and the refusals (the draft's regulation 4 is not visible), are in
-- g8-tests-simplex.l4.  The expectations were decided from the source before any run (work/g8/expectations.md section 6);
-- no value was edited to match the code.  This file doubles as proof that the harness can fail.
-- Each assertion is the table's own claim; an assertion that failed is printed as "assertion failed".

§ `Tests that are meant to fail: what the table says and the text does not`

